BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Survival: Newport's Black History
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
DTSTAMP:20260810T113333Z
UID:57b41b6ae57569530c4fa0a67fb1@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Newport Historical Society (NHS) Walking Tour - Creative Survi
 val: Newport’s Black History Discover the history of Newport’s people 
 of color\, enslaved and free. Explore the places where enslaved people liv
 ed and labored\, along with locations where free African Americans built t
 heir enterprises and supported a new local industry. This tour lasts appro
 ximately 90 mins. Monday\, January 19th at 1:00 PM Sunday\, March 22nd at 
 11:00 AM Monday\, June 1st - Monday\, October 26th at 2:00 PM Health &amp\
 ; Safety As you explore Newport's rich history with us\, please be aware o
 f the following health and safety considerations: Active City Environment:
  Newport is a vibrant\, working city with active traffic and bustling stre
 ets. Please stay alert and follow your guide's instructions at all times. 
 Narrow Streets and Sidewalks: Many of Newport's streets and sidewalks are 
 narrow\, which can sometimes lead to crowded conditions. Please walk singl
 e file when necessary and be cautious when crossing streets. Uneven and Co
 bblestone Surfaces: Sidewalks and streets in historic Newport can be uneve
 n and may include cobblestones. Wear comfortable\, sturdy footwear to navi
 gate these areas safely. Weather Conditions: Newport's weather can be unpr
 edictable. Dress in layers\, wear sun protection\, and bring water to stay
  hydrated\, especially during warm months.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrho
 deisland.com/event/creative-survival%3a-newports-black-history/109644/
LOCATION:Newport Historical Society Walking Tours\, 127 Thames Street\, Ne
 wport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/creative-survival%3a-newports-b
 lack-history/109644/
END:VEVENT
